counterexample:
Open text such as display names, or dynamically user-configured categories loaded at runtime that cannot be known at compile time, need not be compile-time enums. Merely logging or forwarding an external status code at a boundary is not internal state dispatch.
```rust
struct UserProfile {
    display_name: String,
}
```

fix:
Represent a closed state set as an `enum` and convert explicitly at protocol boundaries. Use exhaustive matches where behavior belongs with the variants, or a strategy/polymorphic design when independently extensible behavior warrants it.
```rust
enum ProductStatus {
    NewRelease,
    Regular,
}

struct Product {
    status: ProductStatus,
}
```
